Eighteen entities and nine edges so that the European map shows the
cognitive-engineering and human systems integration (HSI) lineage built
around Guy André Boy and the community linked to him.

Teams (12): ESTIA-Recherche (Bidart), CentraleSupélec LGI (host of the
FlexTech chair), EURISCO 1992–2008 (Toulouse, concluded), ENSC Bordeaux INP
(HAIKU partner, HEAL lab with Thales), Ingenuity i/o (Ingescape), LAMIH
Valenciennes (human–machine cooperation), ETH Zurich Work & Organizational
Psychology (Gudela Grote), AFIS human-factors technical committee, Académie
de l'air et de l'espace, Airbus Defence and Space HSI, Safran Helicopter
Engines (SOMA digital twin), CEAM human factors unit (Mont-de-Marsan).

Projects (2): FlexTech chair 2019–2024 with its industrial consortium;
FlexTech-2 chair 2025–2030 (ESTIA, IRIT, SNCF, Ingenuity i/o).

Frameworks (2): Cognitive Function Analysis & Orchestra model (1998–2013);
Human Systems Integration — TOP model, PRODEC & systemic cognition
(2020–2026), citing Technology in Society 74 (2023) 102298 and
Systems 14(7) (2026) 851.

Commons (2): INCOSE HSI Working Group & conference series (anchored at
Biarritz, HSI2019); HCI-Aero conference series 1986–2016 (concluded).

Also links the HAIKU consortium's Bordeaux INP partner to the new ENSC
entry and adds EN/FR descriptions for every new entity. Sources and
confidence levels are recorded in each entry's provenance; web pages could
only be read through search summaries, so several dates and coordinates
are marked approximate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
