+description: |
+  HCI-Aero was the conference series that Guy André Boy launched in Toulouse in 1986 —
+  first as "Human-Machine Interaction and Artificial Intelligence in Aerospace", renamed
+  HCI-Aero in 1998 — and ran every two years, alternating between Europe and North America,
+  in cooperation with ACM SIGCHI, with EURISCO organising the European editions and AAAI
+  then ACM publishing the proceedings. Its subject was the cockpit and the control room at
+  the moment automation and early AI entered them: authority sharing between crew and
+  automation, cognitive function analysis, intelligent assistants, air-traffic management.
