+  source: 'Boy (2020) Human–Systems Integration: From Virtual to Tangible, CRC Press — https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429351686; Boy & Morel (2022) The machine as a partner: human-machine teaming design using the PRODEC method, Work 73 — https://doi.org/10.3233/WOR-220268; Boy (2023) An epistemological approach to human systems integration, Technology in Society 74, 102298 — https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techsoc.2023.102298; Boy (2026) Systemic Cognition: On the Complexity of Context, Systems 14(7), 851 — https://doi.org/10.3390/systems14070851; Boy (2022) Socioergonomics, arXiv:2201.12344 / INCOSE IS 2022 https://doi.org/10.1002/iis2.12869; Boy, Masson, Durnerin & Morel (2024) PRODEC for HSI of increasingly autonomous systems, Systems Engineering 27(5) — https://doi.org/10.1002/sys.21751; Boy (2025) Systemic Cognition: a few epistemological clarifications, Systems 14(1), 15 — https://doi.org/10.3390/systems14010015; Boy (2020) FlexTech: from rigid to flexible HSI, in Systems Engineering in the Fourth Industrial Revolution (Wiley) — https://doi.org/10.1002/9781119513957.ch18; flextechchair.org; INCOSE HSI Primer press release Oct 2023; web search 2026-09 · timeline.start (high): HSI book, CRC Press, 2020'
