+description: |
+  AFIS, the Association Française d'Ingénierie Système, has been INCOSE's French chapter
+  since 1999 and gathers about a thousand systems engineers from industry, research and
+  public agencies. Its Comité technique Facteurs Humains is the place where human factors
+  and systems engineering are worked together in France: its declared aim is to make the
+  human-centred approach and human–system integration (or human–machine teaming) a
+  recognised systems-engineering practice, through method sheets, webinars and working
+  sessions. It is co-led by practitioners from Airbus Defence and Space and Thales — the
+  same industrial base that funded EURISCO and the FlexTech chair.
+
+  The committee relays Guy André Boy's work to the French systems-engineering community:
+  AFIS webinars presented his book Human–Systems Integration — From Virtual to Tangible and
+  model-based human systems integration of human–AI teams. On this map it is the
+  ecosystem-tier link between the INCOSE HSI working group and the French industrial
+  practitioners who apply HSI to cockpits, mission systems and control rooms.
