+description: |
+  ENSC is the French engineering school of "cognitique" — applied cognitive science and
+  cognitive engineering — created in Bordeaux in 2003 as the Institut de cognitique and part
+  of Bordeaux INP since 2009. It trains engineers with a dual competence in information
+  technology and human sciences, with human factors, human/system integration and the
+  cognitive uses of technology as its core, and its research is carried by the IMS
+  laboratory (UMR CNRS 5218). Since 2009 it has run HEAL, the Human Engineering for
+  Aerospace Lab, a joint laboratory with Thales Avionics and Thales Systèmes Aéroportés
+  on crew workload, anticipation and situation awareness in cockpits.
+
+  On this map it is the Bordeaux INP partner of the Horizon Europe project HAIKU
+  (2022–2025), which built and validated six human-centred AI assistants for cockpits,
+  towers and airports, and the institutional home of the French cognitive-engineering
+  school: the Institut de cognitique was founded in 2003 by Bernard Claverie with Guy
+  André Boy, whose Ingénierie cognitive appeared the same year, and cognitive function
+  analysis is part of its teaching lineage. Jean-Marc Salotti's work on degraded situation awareness and on
+  the human factors of cobotic systems extends the same line to space and manufacturing.
