+description: |
+  ESTIA-Recherche is the research unit of ESTIA, the engineering school of the Basque
+  Country technopole at Bidart, attached to the Université de Bordeaux and a member of
+  Groupe ISAE. Its positioning — durable and empowering interfaces for human–human,
+  human–system and system–system interaction — made it the natural European home of Guy
+  André Boy's human systems integration work when the FlexTech chair was created with
+  CentraleSupélec in 2019: about twenty researchers across the two sites, CIFRE theses with
+  TotalEnergies (a digital twin designed to support situation awareness in remote
+  operations, the Reality Anchor methodology), Safran Helicopter Engines (SOMA, a
+  multi-agent digital twin for engine maintenance), CS Group, the French Air and Space
+  Force (collaborative air combat, virtual assistants) and SNCF, and the PRODEC
+  scenario-based design method.
+
+  The unit also carries the tangible-interaction group (Nadine Couture) and Dimitri
+  Masson's human-centred framework for digital-twin design, so that "tangibility" — a
+  virtual model becoming physically and cognitively graspable by operators — is worked
+  on as a design property rather than a metaphor. ESTIA hosted HSI2019, the first INCOSE
+  international conference on human systems integration, in Biarritz, and the 2024
+  spring school on human–AI teaming; since 2025 it leads the FlexTech-2 chair with IRIT
+  in Toulouse.
