+description: |
+  Gudela Grote's chair of Work and Organizational Psychology at ETH Zurich studies how
+  organisations and teams in high-risk systems manage uncertainty, how standardisation and
+  flexibility trade off, and — increasingly — how AI reshapes work processes and
+  accountability. Its empirical ground is railway operations (Swiss Federal Railways),
+  air-traffic control and healthcare, with field studies feeding automation requirements:
+  the 2016 study of en-route controllers showed that automation must support rather than
+  remove the controllers' own strategies for handling uncertainty.
+
+  The chair is the Swiss anchor of Guy André Boy's network: Boy and Grote co-authored the
+  work on authority in increasingly complex human–machine collaborative systems, applied to
+  the evolution of air-traffic management (IEA 2009) and the "authority issue in
+  organizational automation" chapter of Boy's 2011 handbook, ETH hosted the announcement
+  of the first INCOSE HSI conference, and Grote taught at the FlexTech spring school on
+  human–AI teaming in 2024. On this map it represents the organisational side of human
+  systems integration — who holds authority when a system becomes more autonomous.
