+  Ingenuity i/o is a Toulouse software company founded in 2012 by Stéphane Valès, an
+  ENAC-trained air-traffic and computer engineer from the French aeronautical
+  human-computer interaction community. Its product, Ingescape, is a model-based framework
+  for distributed interactive software: agents, displays, 2D/3D interaction devices and
+  simulators are described and orchestrated without a central broker, so that a control
+  position, a cockpit or a supervision room can be prototyped and re-wired quickly, and
+  the same models feed verification and human-factors evaluation.
+
+  It sits on this map because it is the tooling partner of the human systems integration
+  community: Ingescape was the platform on which the FlexTech chair ran its
+  human-in-the-loop simulations and PRODEC scenarios, it was taught at the 2024 spring
+  school on human–AI teaming, and the company is a founding industrial member of the
+  FlexTech-2 chair led by ESTIA and IRIT.
