+description: |
+  Safran Helicopter Engines, headquartered at Bordes near Pau, is the world's leading
+  helicopter-engine maker and runs its main production and R&D site there, transformed since
+  2010 under a "factory of the future" programme. Its place on this map comes from a
+  human systems integration project run with the FlexTech chair: SOMA, a multi-agent,
+  self-learning digital twin designed to support collaborative decision-making in
+  helicopter-engine maintenance. Rather than an automated prescriptive-maintenance engine,
+  SOMA coordinates human and artificial agents through stigmergy — each leaves traces the
+  others use — so that maintenance professionals keep the decision while the twin
+  accumulates and redistributes the knowledge.
+
+  The work was a CIFRE thesis at ESTIA supervised within the chair (INCOSE International
+  Symposium 2022, Springer 2025), prototyped and tested with the Bordes maintenance teams;
+  Safran Helicopter Engines is also a historic partner of the ESTIA foundation. It
+  illustrates HSI applied to industrial maintenance: a digital twin built as a partner in
+  a decision, with tangibility and function allocation designed in from the start.
